## [AWS Security Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/what-is-securityhub-v2.md)

- [Concepts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-concepts.md): Describes Security Hub concepts.

### [Cost Estimator](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/security-hub-cost-estimator.md)

Describes Security Hub cost estimator

- [Setting up cross-account access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/setting-up-cross-account-access.md): You can configure cross-account access for the cost estimator
- [Using the cost estimator](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/using-cost-estimator.md): You can access the Cost Estimator from multiple locations in the AWS Management Console.

### [Enabling Security Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-enable.md)

Describes how to enable Security Hub.

- [Designating a delegated administrator](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-set-da.md): Describes how to set a delegated administrator in Security Hub.
- [Creating the delegated administrator policy](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-policy-statement.md): Create a policy allowing the delegated administrator to configure Security Hub and perform actions in AWS Organizations.
- [Managing configuration of member accounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-da-policy.md): Describes how to enable a policy as the delegated administrator
- [Removing a delegated administrator](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-remove-da.md): Describes how to remove the delegated administrator in Security Hub.
- [Re-enabling Security Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-reenable.md): Describes how to re-enable Security Hub.
- [Recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-recommendations.md): Learn about AWS services to enable with Security Hub
- [Account coverage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/security-hub-account-coverage.md): Use the account coverage page and security coverage widget to track which accounts and Regions are covered by security capabilities.
- [Extended plan](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-extended-plan.md): Learn about the Security Hub Extended plan, which provides integrated partner security solutions with flexible pricing and no long-term commitments.

### [Cross-Region aggregation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/security-hub-region-aggregation.md)

Cross-Region aggregation allows you to aggregate findings, resources, and trends from multiple AWS Regions into a single home Region.

- [Enabling aggregation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/sh-finding-aggregation-enable.md): Enable cross-Region aggregation in Security Hub from the home Region.
- [Reviewing aggregation settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/sh-finding-aggregation-view-config.md): Review your current cross-Region aggregation settings in Security Hub.
- [Updating aggregation settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/sh-finding-aggregation-update.md): Update your cross-Region aggregation settings in Security Hub by changing the linked Regions or whether to link new Regions.
- [Deleting aggregation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/sh-finding-aggregation-delete.md): Delete cross-Region aggregation of findings in Security Hub

### [Integration with Azure](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-azure.md)

Learn how to integrate AWS Security Hub with Microsoft Azure for posture management, vulnerability management, and threat detection.

- [Prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-azure-prereqs.md): Learn which permissions and resources you need before creating a connector in AWS Security Hub.
- [Configuring Azure](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-azure-setup-azure.md): Learn how to configure your Microsoft Azure environment to support integration with AWS Security Hub.
- [Configuring Security Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-azure-setup-securityhub-v2.md): Learn how to create a connector and configure AWS Security Hub to monitor your Azure resources.
- [Deleting an Azure connector](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-azure-delete.md): Learn how to delete an Microsoft Azure connector in AWS Security Hub and what happens to your existing findings and resources.

### [Summary dashboard](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/dashboard-v2.md)

Learn about the summary dashboard in AWS Security Hub.

- [Viewing details about resources in Security Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/resource-view.md): The Resources page tracks common resources across your account and organization.

### [Finding format: OCSF](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-ocsf.md)

Learn about OCSF and how it is used with Security Hub

### [AWS extension for OCSF](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/ocsf-aws-extension.md)

Learn about the AWS extension for OCSF.

- [Basic attributes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/aws-extension-basic-attributes.md): Learn about the basic attributes in the AWS extension for OCSF used for resource identification, location, and metadata.
- [Resource specific objects](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/aws-extension-resource-specific-objects.md): Learn about the resource-specific objects in the AWS extension for OCSF that provide detailed information for specific resource types.
- [Coverage findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/coverage-findings.md): Describes coverage findings.
- [AI Inventory](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-ai-inventory.md): Learn how the AI inventory in AWS Security Hub provides a unified view of managed and self-hosted AI and ML resources across your AWS environment.

### [Exposure findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings.md)

Learn how exposure findings in AWS Security Hub can help you identify and respond to the highest-priority risks in your AWS environment.

- [Supported resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-supported-resources.md): Learn which AWS resource types support the generation of exposure findings in AWS Security Hub.
- [Supported traits](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-supported-traits.md): Learn which exposure traits Security Hub uses to generate exposure findings.

### [Generating exposure findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-generate.md)

Learn how AWS Security Hub generates new exposure findings in your account.

- [Sample exposure finding](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-sample.md): Shows an example of an exposure finding.
- [Determining the severity level of an exposure finding](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-severity.md): Learn about severity levels in AWS Security Hub

### [Reviewing exposure findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-review.md)

Review your exposure findings in AWS Security Hub.

- [Reviewing details for exposure findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-review-details.md): This topic describes how to review details about exposure findings in the AWS Security Hub console and with the API.
- [Potential attack path graph](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/potential-attack-path-graph.md): Learn about the potential attack path graph in AWS Security Hub.

### [Remediating exposure findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-findings-remediate.md)

The topics in this section describe remediation steps for exposure findings across different AWS services.

- [Remediating exposures for DynamoDB tables](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-ddb-instance.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for DynamoDB tables.
- [Remediating exposures for EC2 instances](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-ec2-instance.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) instances.
- [Remediating exposures for Amazon ECS services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-ecs-service.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) services.
- [Remediating exposures for Amazon EKS clusters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-eks-cluster.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters.
- [Remediating exposures for IAM users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-iam-user.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) users.
- [Remediating exposures for AWS Lambda functions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-lambda-function.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for AWS Lambda functions.
- [Remediating exposures for Amazon RDS instances and clusters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-rds.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon RDS instances and clusters.
- [Remediating exposures for Amazon S3 buckets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-s3-bucket.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) buckets.
- [Remediating exposures for Amazon SageMaker notebook instances](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-sagemaker-notebook-instance.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Amazon SageMaker notebook instances.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure virtual machines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-virtual-machine.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure virtual machines.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Storage blob containers](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-storage-blob-container.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Storage blob containers.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure SQL databases](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-sql-database.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure SQL databases.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Cosmos DB accounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-cosmos-db.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Cosmos DB accounts.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Function apps](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-function.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Function apps.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Container apps](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-container-app.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Container apps.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Kubernetes Service clusters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-container-managed-cluster.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters.
- [Remediating exposures for Azure Graph users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/exposure-azure-graph-user.md): AWS Security Hub can generate exposure findings for Azure Graph users.
- [Unused access findings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/unused-access-findings.md): Learn how Security Hub uses IAM Access Analyzer to identify unused IAM permissions, roles, access keys, and passwords.
- [Policy recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/unused-access-recommendations.md): Learn how to generate least-privilege policy recommendations for unused permissions findings in Security Hub.
- [Network Scanning](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-network-scanning.md): Learn about Network Scanning in Security Hub, which performs active network reachability testing on your cloud resources.
- [Remediation plans](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-v2-remediation-plans.md): Learn how remediation plans in AWS Security Hub group exposure findings that share a cause, such as one misconfigured resource.

